<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I47d5449585a2d64641c211a8da7f63c26906fc71" commit="074a8bc1b7f13af9992def71ba8ee2e846c737d7" commit_message="pack_firmware: Correct two pylint warnings  Fix the following warningsin pack_firmware_unittest:  C:155, 0: Wrong continued indentation. C:476, 2: Variable args/keywords are named *args/**kwargs, not _  BUG=chromium:754212 TEST=PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_unittest.py &amp;&amp; \ PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_functest.py  Signed-off-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I47d5449585a2d64641c211a8da7f63c26906fc71 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/625691 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="625691" owner_email="sjg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/91/625691/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id73d7e2f6fd8193036001f642965ff5f7cb3228c" commit="aa9c9dfcebea863bbd020a53aa7cf74818a8d15b" commit_message="pack_firmware: Write a signing config file  For unified builds we need to tell the signer which images to sign and which keys to use for each. This appears in a new 'signer_config.csv' file in the firmware update shellball.  Add support for this.  BUG=b:64842314 BUG=chromium:741043 TEST=PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_unittest.py &amp;&amp; \ PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_functest.py  Change-Id: Id73d7e2f6fd8193036001f642965ff5f7cb3228c Signed-off-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/624463 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="624463" owner_email="sjg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/63/624463/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1351a4d9bbf1f2ec2e33e8c2059f0c0838d5f928" commit="7332038f66f337ba2d41202fe612cc98e66d959c" commit_message="pack_firmware: Drop the KEYSET_DIR variable  This is not a per-model setting so should not be included in the setvars.sh script. Instead each model has its own key id. Drop this old incorrect variable.  BUG=b:64842314 BUG=chromium:741043 TEST=PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_unittest.py &amp;&amp; \ PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_functest.py  Change-Id: I1351a4d9bbf1f2ec2e33e8c2059f0c0838d5f928 Signed-off-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/625689 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="625689" owner_email="sjg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/89/625689/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I99755f0f5a3673c52cdb5293d00f168345aa7a26" commit="669653a4f0e16a39a8834caeef8b4d5dbe7114c5" commit_message="FROMLIST: HID: multitouch: report MT_TOOL_PALM for non-confident touches  According to Microsoft specification [1] for Precision Touchpads (and Touchscreens) the devices use &quot;confidence&quot; reports to signal accidental touches, or contacts that are &quot;too large to be a finger&quot;. Instead of simply marking contact inactive in this case (which causes issues if contact was originally proper and we lost confidence in it later, as this results in accidental clicks, drags, etc), let's report such contacts as MT_TOOL_PALM and let userspace decide what to do. Additionally, let's report contact size for such touches as maximum allowed for major/minor, which should help userspace that is not yet aware of MT_TOOL_PALM to still perform palm rejection.  An additional complication, is that some firmwares do not report non-confident touches as active. To cope with this we delay release of such contact (i.e. if contact was active we first report it as still active MT+TOOL_PALM and then synthesize the release event in a separate frame).  [1] https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/design/component-guidelines/touchpad-windows-precision-touchpad-collection  Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt;  BUG=b:38045083 TEST=Build and boot Eve, try using touchscreen/touchpad  (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9894803/) Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I99755f0f5a3673c52cdb5293d00f168345aa7a26 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/617811 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="617811" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/11/617811/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ia2519f8a1fcb6430f13e8e6e691ddf87144eb198" commit="193dc075fedcfc5b23fb39542bcc77929c5b2ed6" commit_message="FROMLIST: HID: multitouch: touchscreens also use confidence reports  According to [1] the confidence is used not only by touchpad devices, but also by touchscreens.  [1] https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-hardware/design/component-guidelines/touchscreen-required-hid-top-level-collections  Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dmitry.torokhov@gmail.com&gt;  BUG=b:38045083 TEST=Build and boot Eve, try using touchscreen/touchpad  (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9894799/) Signed-off-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ia2519f8a1fcb6430f13e8e6e691ddf87144eb198 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/617812 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="617812" owner_email="dtor@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/617812/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I075eda3674df1d4cd4a23b60e99ebc3a04f0a82b" commit="43dc810b22387da1c9d79c73517f8ae6843b3b6c" commit_message="increase visibility of reportig of the downloaded image version  When using xbuddy:// naming scheme and specifying &quot;latest&quot; in the argument, it is not clear what version is actually being retrieved from the server.  Let's increase visibility of the log message informing user what's coming to his device.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=ran the following command:    $ cros flash ssh://172.22.30.129 xbuddy://remote/reef/latest-dev/test      observed the following in the log:    16:40:59: NOTICE: Using image reef-release/R62-9868.0.0/chromiumos_test_image.bin  Change-Id: I075eda3674df1d4cd4a23b60e99ebc3a04f0a82b Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/627627 Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="627627" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/27/627627/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id3711bbe73dfe652184bc046b5f642c30b8d1627" commit="7c9a23d23439ebd062139a4a780dc1ca0f6a9ec0" commit_message="[unibuild] Support for unibuild firmware signing  For design context, see go/cros-unibuild-signing  This adds support for multiple, shared firmware images from a unified build that needs to be signed with different OEM specific keys.  It uses a signer_config.csv file (that is generated by pack_firmware.py) to determine which images need to be signed with which keys.  BUG=b:64842314 TEST=./build_image --board=coral dev &amp;&amp; ./mod_image_for_recovery.sh --board=coral &amp;&amp; ~/trunk/src/platform/vboot_reference/scripts/image_signing/sign_official_build.sh recovery ../build/images/coral/latest/recovery_image.bin ../platform/vboot_reference/tests/devkeys BRANCH=None  Change-Id: Id3711bbe73dfe652184bc046b5f642c30b8d1627 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/626718 Commit-Ready: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Tested-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="626718" owner_email="shapiroc@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/18/626718/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaeaddad223f35f0e5cad1549b85fa3f7e4d5e1c7" commit="844c606ecd91edbafed152931dd5f9ca1b09c167" commit_message="sweetberry: modify powerlog.py to support multiple devices  powerlog.py can now take -A serialA -B serialB to collect data from both left and right sweetberries simultaneously.  Also, the Spower class has been modified to allow API usage rather than console only usage.  BRANCH=None BUG=chromium:608039 TEST=log from both sweetberries on marlin  Signed-off-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Iaeaddad223f35f0e5cad1549b85fa3f7e4d5e1c7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/422496 Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;a